          </article>

          <article class="proof-story briefing-story" data-scenario-event="scenario_patient_briefing">
            <figure><img src="/assets/home-v3-dog-focus-timeline.png" alt="Household events becoming a concise local timeline" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy" /></figure>
            <div class="proof-copy">
              <p class="eyebrow">Keep the day without interrupting it</p>
              <h2>Most of the day can wait until you are home.</h2>
              <p>Routine motion, the dog on the sofa, and an open window do not all deserve a push notification. HarborNavi keeps the day in order, lets configured urgent conditions reach you, and saves the calm version for when you walk in.</p>
              <div class="briefing-list">
                <div><time>2:14 PM</time><span>Package delivered</span></div>
                <div><time>4:32 PM</time><span>One pet moment kept</span></div>
                <div><time>5:08 PM</time><span>Living-room window open for 18 minutes</span></div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="proof-story movie-story" data-scenario-event="scenario_natural_language_action">
            <div class="proof-copy">
              <p class="eyebrow">Ask before guessing</p>
              <h2>&quot;Movie night&quot; changes the plan for the room.</h2>
              <p>Start with the result. HarborNavi can clarify which room and devices you mean, map the Home Assistant, Zigbee, and IR paths available in the setup, and make a temporary exception understandable before it runs.</p>
              <div class="conversation" aria-label="Example movie night conversation">
                <p class="from-user"><span>You</span>Movie night.</p>
                <p><span>HarborNavi</span>Living-room TV, lights at 20%, AC at 72&deg;F?</p>
                <p class="from-user"><span>You</span>Yes, and mute routine alerts for two hours.</p>
                <strong>4 devices &middot; 1 temporary exception &middot; Ready</strong>
              </div>
            </div>
            <figure><img src="/assets/home-v4-movie-night-workflow.png" alt="A movie-night request coordinating lighting, television, and climate devices" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy" /></figure>
          </article>

          <aside class="trust-strip">
            <div><p class="eyebrow">A clear local boundary</p><h2>Access changes still wait for you.</h2></div>
            <p>Adding a member, expanding room permissions, or pairing a Bluetooth or Zigbee device changes who can see or control the home. Planned fingerprint confirmation keeps those setup changes at the box. Everyday questions and routines stay easy.</p>
            <img src="/assets/home-v4-trust-boundary.png" alt="Local fingerprint confirmation for a sensitive household access change" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy" />
